      ],
      "title": "Parse actual native machine configuration before qualifying XT/640KB coverage",
      "detail": "validate_candidate checks a fixed result.machine dictionary and that result.config matches the hashed config file, but never parses that config. An actual640C config changed from cpu_family8088/mem_size640 to386/1024 stillpasses when theconfig/result hashes are refreshed and the declared result.machine dictionary is left unchanged. The existing wrong-RAM negative test changes only the declaration, so it misses this mismatch. This gate can accept evidence from a different or invalid machine while claiming normal XT/640KB.",
      "reproduction": "Import VERIFY.PY, load CANDIDATE.JSN, positive validate_candidate passes. Copy640C result/config in memory; edit actualconfig cpu_family/mem_size, update result.config and rowconfig/result identities, leave result.machine unchanged; substitute only those2blobs through V.exact; validate_candidate returns normally. No repository/guest file changed.",
      "observed": "BAD_HARDWARE_CONFIGURATION_ACCEPTED",
      "fix": "Parse Machine and Video sections from exact(row.config), enforce8088/4772728/ibmxt86/640/cga plus no dynarec/extra-memory override, and compare parsed values with the native declaration. Add negative tests altering actualconfig while restamping its identities and keeping declaration unchanged.",
      "scope": "Actual recorded320C/640C configurations were inspected and are correct. Finding is a fail-closed qualification boundary defect, not evidence that those runs used wrong hardware."
    }
  ],
